WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.033
-Our next guest can be seen

00:00:02.033 --> 00:00:03.767
at the Denver Comedy Works South

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:05.801
February 10th through the 12th.

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:08.801
Please welcome the very funny Matthew Broussard.

00:00:08.801 --> 00:00:10.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:17.300
♪♪

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.834
-Thank you very much. Thank you so much.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:22.734
Appreciate that.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.667
Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:25.901
Y'all doing good?

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.033
[ Cheers and applause ] Awesome. I'm doing great.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.434
My girlfriend and I just celebrated five years together.

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.634
Five years. Thank you very much.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.734
Yes, we're fighting less now.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.334
We did two things.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.033
We learned each other's love languages.

00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:39.968
I recommend that. There's five of them.

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:43.901
They're gifts, words, service, time, and affection.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:45.300
My love language is words.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.200
Her love language is gifts, words, service,

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.634
time, and affection.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.567
Yahtzee. Yes.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:55.067
We also got a cat. He is the love our life.

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:58.934
[ Cheers and applause ] Yes. His name is Password.

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.434
My girlfriend works in cybersecurity,

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:04.901
and the most commonly used password is your pet's name,

00:01:04.901 --> 00:01:08.501
and I didn't feel like changing mine, so Password -- it stays.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.868
[ Laughter ] Thank you.

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:12.934
She has a great job, my girlfriend. She works in tech.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:15.968
I made a mistake recently. I looked at her tax documents.

00:01:15.968 --> 00:01:18.801
I learned she makes four times what I do.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:23.567
So I am a feminist, yes. That's what that makes me.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:25.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.234
Yeah. People are like, "What kind of feminist are you?

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:29.067
Intersectional? Third wave?"

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:32.868
I'm like, "Indentured? I don't know."

00:01:32.868 --> 00:01:35.868
I'm fighting for my maternity leave. You understand?

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:37.834
I'm not trying to rely on her financially,

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:40.234
but in case of emergency, break the glass ceiling.

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:43.033
That's my bumper sticker that I put on my laptop

00:01:43.033 --> 00:01:44.367
because I don't own a car.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:46.367
And it's a weird feeling.

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:48.334
I've always struggled to find a balance

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:51.100
between being a good boyfriend and my job,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.734
and now being a good boyfriend is my job.

00:01:54.734 --> 00:01:57.300
I'm only here because she approved my PTO.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.868
I'm on call right now.

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:02.334
And I love comedy.

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:05.000
I mean, "Tonight Show" is a dream come true.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.868
But because of her income,

00:02:07.868 --> 00:02:09.934
this is just a cute hobby.

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.334
That's all this is.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:13.133
Everything I'm doing could be summed up

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.834
by her at a dinner party being like,

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.334
"Honey, honey, come show them your little trick.

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.467
Come on. Do one of your little skits.

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:22.400
Isn't that precious?"

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.067
It's changed my motivations.

00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:27.567
I used to work out for fitness. Now I work out for job security.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:29.901
I got to keep this ass tight.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:32.000
If I get shredded, so does the prenup.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.667
That's my thinspo.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:37.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:41.033
She has not figured out how much power she now has over me.

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:44.434
She asked me recently, "Would you ever leave me?"

00:02:44.434 --> 00:02:47.701
And I said, "It would have to be a competitive offer.

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:50.133
I'm not jumping ship for nothing."

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:52.734
Not trying to be some entry level F-boy

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:55.434
freelancing with no health insurance.

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:58.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.701
She wasn't making a lot of money when we first started dating.

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:03.601
At that point, she was a professional athlete.

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:05.868
I was not. I'm not very good at sports.

00:03:05.868 --> 00:03:08.267
I know I look like I played lacrosse for Slytherin.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:12.968
But I'm not a coordinated person.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:15.868
She was a swimmer, and we had kind of a rocky start.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:18.067
Two months after we started dating,

00:03:18.067 --> 00:03:19.834
she went to the U.S. Olympic trials.

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:22.534
She was a top contender to make the Olympic team,

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.133
and she didn't.

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:26.334
And it is very painful when a person

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:30.067
works their whole life at one goal and misses,

00:03:30.067 --> 00:03:33.501
and you've only been dating that person for two months.

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:37.167
That was a lot for me to deal with on our seventh date.

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:38.868
What do you say to that?

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:40.734
Be like, "Hey, sorry you failed at your dreams.

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:42.400
Also what's your middle name?

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.567
Mine's Lawrence. Isn't that embarrassing?"

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:46.968
"Do you have any food allergies?

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:49.601
Do you believe in God? Anymore?"

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:51.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:53.901
Thank you.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:56.133
Also, I thought she was going to make the team,

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:57.601
which means she would go to the Olympics,

00:03:57.601 --> 00:03:59.200
but she would also go to the Olympic village,

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.300
which is famously debaucherous.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.934
It's all of the best athletes in the world

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.133
partying, drinking, romance.

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:09.100
And my brother asked me, "What if she cheats on you?"

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:12.100
And I said, "Well, then she better get pregnant,

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.400
because whatever she pops out,

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.534
I will raise like my flesh and blood.

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:19.901
I will be the proudest dad at field day."

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.367
Like, "That's my son!"

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:24.167
And people are like, "Looks a lot like Usain Bolt."

00:04:24.167 --> 00:04:26.300
I'm like, "Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.634
People said that about me at that age. They did."

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:31.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:33.601
Thank you.

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:35.334
Here's the twist.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:36.801
I've been doing comedy for ten years.

00:04:36.801 --> 00:04:38.501
I've been dating her for five years.

00:04:38.501 --> 00:04:42.334
One year ago, she started doing comedy, as well.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:45.434
Which means she watched me do this for four years

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:48.167
and was like, "Seems easy enough. Alright.

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:49.801
If this clown can do it, scoot over."

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.501
I always wanted my work to be inspiring

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:55.167
but not in a "Rudy" kind of way.

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:57.000
And she was very secretive about it.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:59.400
She wouldn't let me watch,

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.367
and then we got booked on a show together.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.033
And I was a little nervous for her,

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:05.734
and I got to see her perform, and it was awesome.

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:07.634
Because she's good. She's really good.

00:05:07.634 --> 00:05:11.567
But she's also not as good as me, which --

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.767
Whew! Thank God!

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:18.267
Strong act, but don't quit our day job.

00:05:18.267 --> 00:05:21.200
Someone has to pay 3/4ths of the rent around here.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:22.834
Hey, thank you so much.

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:24.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:27.000
♪♪

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.601
-Ah! Fantastic. Come on.

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:35.200
Matthew Broussard! Matthew Broussard.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:37.868
He'll be at the Denver Comedy Works South

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:39.300
February 10th through the 12th.

